// The value of an initializer is written in the context of the parent, and keeps its temporal
// meaning there (gsdlab/clafer#123): X (some flag) is about the next state of the Box, an
// obligation that lasts as long as the parent of Box, the root. A Box that disappears in the
// next state has no flag then, so x starts at 2. In the context of x, the obligation would
// lapse with the Box, and x would start at 1.

Box ?
    flag ?
    x -> integer := if X (some flag) then 1 else 2
[ initially (some Box && X no Box) ]

assert [ initially (Box.x = 2) ]
